ghidra-decompiler

This crate is a Rust port of the Ghidra decompiler and embeds SLEIGH language files
from Ghidra (commit d6192cb3f9, https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra).
The notice of Ghidra follows.

Ghidra-derived confirmed-call analysis

The native worker's bounded direct-call function discovery adapts the confirmed
call and call-to-fallthrough exclusion rules from Ghidra's FunctionAnalyzer.java:
https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/blob/9a723ce99952771b8368329503aa589ae233e916/Ghidra/Features/Base/src/main/java/ghidra/app/plugin/core/function/FunctionAnalyzer.java

Upstream revision: 9a723ce99952771b8368329503aa589ae233e916
License: Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).
Rust adaptations use the desktop's immutable image model and public engine APIs,
with explicit work budgets, session-only call references, and worker progress.
This is separate from the pinned decompiler port and its Ghidra source revision.

Ghidra function-start patterns

data/function-starts/x86-64gcc_patterns.xml and x86-64win_patterns.xml are
copied unchanged from Ghidra's Processors/x86/data/patterns at revision
9a723ce99952771b8368329503aa589ae233e916. src/function_patterns.rs adapts the
pattern-pair, ditted-bit, alignment and funcstart semantics of Ghidra's
FunctionStartAnalyzer.java and PatternPairSet.java:
https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/blob/9a723ce99952771b8368329503aa589ae233e916/Ghidra/Features/BytePatterns/src/main/java/ghidra/app/analyzers/FunctionStartAnalyzer.java
https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/blob/9a723ce99952771b8368329503aa589ae233e916/Ghidra/Features/Base/src/main/java/ghidra/util/bytesearch/PatternPairSet.java

License: Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).
The Rust adaptation admits only funcstart actions, requires each candidate's
code to decode completely outside established code, and uses bounded,
resumable scanning instead of the Java Program database.

Ghidra-derived address-table recovery

src/code_pointers.rs, src/analysis/pointers.rs and
src/analysis/function_candidates.rs adapt aligned pointer-run search,
relocation guidance, executable-target and offcut/collision checks from:
https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/blob/8ca9077040cc43cd790babcfccf19475622a3e9a/Ghidra/Features/Base/src/main/java/ghidra/app/plugin/core/disassembler/AddressTableAnalyzer.java
https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/blob/8ca9077040cc43cd790babcfccf19475622a3e9a/Ghidra/Features/Base/src/main/java/ghidra/app/plugin/core/disassembler/AddressTable.java
https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/blob/8ca9077040cc43cd790babcfccf19475622a3e9a/Ghidra/Features/BytePatterns/src/main/java/ghidra/app/analyzers/FunctionStartAnalyzer.java

Upstream revision: 8ca9077040cc43cd790babcfccf19475622a3e9a (Ghidra 12.2).
License: Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).
Ghidra's AddressTableAnalyzer leaves function creation disabled. This adaptation
adds independent ELF FDE/pattern corroboration, bounded complete CFG validation,
resumable parent-owned work and in-memory admission witnesses. The small ELF
init/fini and FDE-range reader is an independent implementation, not an unwinder.
Existing vendored pattern data retains its separate revision above.

Ghidra named no-return functions

The three data/no-return/*FunctionsThatDoNotReturn files are copied unchanged
from Ghidra/Features/Base/data at revision
9a723ce99952771b8368329503aa589ae233e916. src/no_return.rs adapts the container
selection and leading-underscore name matching of NoReturnFunctionAnalyzer.java:
https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/blob/9a723ce99952771b8368329503aa589ae233e916/Ghidra/Features/Base/src/main/java/ghidra/app/plugin/core/analysis/NoReturnFunctionAnalyzer.java

License: Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).
The native policy excludes returning/ABI-sensitive entries, adds two documented
ELF entries, uses exact import-slot/thunk evidence, and does not infer wrappers.
Provenance and file hashes are recorded in data/no-return/README.md.

Ghidra-derived direct-memory reference analysis

The bounded data-access pass adapts direct-memory reference rules from the COPY,
LOAD and STORE cases, and constant-transfer and unknown-output rules for integer
arithmetic, extension, PIECE/SUBPIECE and calls, from Ghidra's
SymbolicPropogator.java:
https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/blob/9a723ce99952771b8368329503aa589ae233e916/Ghidra/Features/Base/src/main/java/ghidra/program/util/SymbolicPropogator.java

Upstream revision: 9a723ce99952771b8368329503aa589ae233e916
License: Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).
The Rust adaptation uses public instruction p-code, file-backed range validation,
bounded work and session-only evidence. AArch64 propagation is limited to
concrete register constants within one basic block; it omits symbolic values,
memory modeling, cross-block flow and the Java Program database, and retains the
upstream Ghidra notices below.

src/data_analysis.rs also records address formation (address-taking references).
It adapts the COPY, STORE and INT_ADD pointer-value handling, the small-value
offset check and the stored-value reference rules of SymbolicPropogator.java in
Ghidra 12.2, revision 8ca9077040cc43cd790babcfccf19475622a3e9a, inspected in
Ghidra/Features/Base/lib/Base-src.zip of the ghidra_12.2_PUBLIC distribution:
ghidra/program/util/SymbolicPropogator.java (COPY, STORE and INT_ADD cases,
checkPossibleOffsetAddr, addStoredReferences, makeReference)
ghidra/app/plugin/core/analysis/ScalarOperandAnalyzer.java (addReference)
ghidra/app/plugin/core/analysis/OperandReferenceAnalyzer.java (reference
iteration; consulted for side effects that are deliberately not imported)

License: Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).
The Rust adaptation evaluates public engine p-code only. It records final
pointer-width general-register values and concrete stored pointer values that
name one file-backed byte at or above 0x1000, x86 within one instruction and
AArch64 within one basic block. ADRP page bases are never published alone.
Unlike Ghidra it does not speculate on scalar operands, consult symbols or
existing references, create data definitions, disassemble or create functions at
targets, or chase loaded pointers. No Ghidra source or Java runtime is included.

----

The desktop's ARM64 PE runtime-metadata reader is an independent implementation
of Microsoft's documented ARM64 exception-handling binary format:
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/build/arm64-exception-handling?view=msvc-170
It is separate from Ghidra's Java auto-analysis framework. Its original synthetic
fixtures and exact import-veneer recognizer use the pinned engine's public APIs.

